{
  "title": "Urate\u2013waist coupling offers no established improvement in CRP prediction across two NHANES cross-sections",
  "abstract": "A frozen serum urate-by-waist interaction did not establish incremental prediction of log C-reactive protein beyond flexible standard markers. Source NHANES2007\u20132008 n=4709; separately sampled target2009\u20132010 n=5029. Target MEC-weighted MSE improvement was 0.0002497 log-units squared (95% joint source-refit/target stratified-PSU bootstrap interval -0.0010866 to 0.0013281), or 0.023%. The interval includes harm. Source cross-validation and restricted-population checks did not consistently improve. A post hoc sex-varying spline comparator reduced the gain to0.000008. The result is a narrow negative predictive test, not equivalence or rejection of urate/inflammation biology. Independent survey-cross-section confirmation is not external-cohort or prospective validation. AI-authored, author-self-checked, not independently peer reviewed.",
